    <description><![CDATA[A beautiful client for Plex & Jellyfin

Stream your media library with HDR, Dolby Vision, offline downloads, and a gorgeous experience across all your devices.

**Features**

- Wide Codec Support
- HDR10+
- Subtitles
- Cross-Platform
- Offline
- Watch Together
- Tracker Sync
- Skip intros
- Chapter support
- Gestures
]]></description>
    <summary>A modern client for Plex and Jellyfin on desktop, mobile, and TV. Built with Flutter for native performance and a clean interface.</summary>
    <releaseNotes><![CDATA[[Releases](https://github.com/edde746/plezy/releases)

Public beta of Plezy 3.0: Plezy rebuilt as a native app on every platform.

**Read before installing:** on Android, Mac and Windows this beta installs over Plezy 2.x and upgrades its data, one way. To go back, uninstall the beta, reinstall 2.x and sign in again.

Install notes, known limitations, how to report bugs and the vote on how 3.0 should ship are in the pinned announcement issue: #3165.

SHA256SUMS lists the checksum of every file.

## Changes since beta 1

- TV: library grids use the 2.x sizes again and scroll more smoothly
- Android TV: Watch Next artwork shows in launchers
- Windows: starts when Credential Manager is full (#3169)
- Item menus in a clearer order (#3171)
- Season chips show watch progress (#3172)
- Season cards open the show with that season selected
- iPad: Libraries no longer freezes the app
- Home: shortcut chips start with Live TV and your libraries
- Downloads is its own page: a tab on phones, a sidebar entry elsewhere
- Computers: rows fade at their edges and scroll with the mouse wheel, by dragging, or with ‹ › buttons
- Mac: one universal build that also runs on Intel Macs
- Crash reports are now sent to Plezy's own server (bugs.plezy.app)]]></releaseNotes>
